    Fix workspace archive cleanup retries (#5091)
    
    ## Summary
    
    - record when finished-job workspace packaging has succeeded and which
    source directories it consumed
    - retry only source cleanup after a post-packaging failure instead of
    packaging the now-empty directories again
    - preserve the existing workspace-save retry log contract and
    distinguish persistent cleanup failures from archive-write failures
    - add helper-level and completion-loop regression coverage
    
    ## Root cause
    
    `FilesystemStorage._write_multi` moves workspace contents into the
    job-store archive. If the later `shutil.rmtree` failed, `JobRunner`
    retried the whole operation. That retry repackaged emptied source
    directories and replaced the complete archive with an empty ZIP, while
    the job could still be published as `FINISHED:COMPLETED`.
    
    ## Impact
    
    A successful archive can no longer be overwritten by a cleanup retry.
    Cleanup remains retryable within the existing grace period, and
    completed job artifacts remain downloadable.
    
    ## Validation
    
    - `tests/unit_test/private/fed/server/job_runner_test.py`: 39 passed
    - job definition manager and filesystem storage tests: 36 passed
    - `tests/unit_test/private/fed/server`: 410 passed
    - scoped Black, isort, flake8, and `git diff --check`: passed
    - unchanged DLQASH MR !195 production/subprocess reproducer on Colossus,
    1 server + 2 clients:
      - pytest RC 0
      - archive peak/final: 95,017 == 95,017 bytes
      - job reached `FINISHED:COMPLETED`
    - `download_job` succeeded with intact, nonempty workspace/model
    artifacts
    - cleanup retried 18 times while workspace packaging occurred exactly
    once
    - persistent-failure grace-bound and transient-recovery companion cases:
    2 passed
